 *   **When to Use:** When training large-scale unbounded scenes where structural continuity is critical and Gaussian overfitting is observed [S1].
 
 ## Background
-Cross-View Consistent Loss was introduced in the context of Gaussian Splatting for large-scale unbounded scenes to reinforce structural continuity and avoid rendering artifacts [S1]. It builds upon the idea that structural features are limited by resolution, thus requiring cross-view consistency to refine scene representation [S1]. The method was proposed in "SplatCo: Structure-View Collaborative Gaussian Splatting for Detail-Preserving Rendering of Large-Scale Unbounded Scenes" [S1].
